 August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 158% of normal in May to June and 45% in September to October. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 47% and February to March at 44%. Grid 15441 had its driest year in 1956 at 52%.</p>"}
